<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB Q1 net rises 7.8 pct.</title>
<headline>ABB Q1 net rises 7.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>First quarter 1997 vs first</p>
<p>quarter 1996:	   (million U.S. dollars unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net income	     236		 vs 219</p>
<p>Operating earnings after</p>
<p> depreciation		   472		 vs 425</p>
<p> New orders		     10,076	    vs 8,720</p>
<p> Revenue			  7,018	     vs 7,256</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name is ABB Asea Brown Boveri AG. ABB said in its quarterly statement that it no longer included imputed interest income on advances. It therefore had restated orders, revenues, operating earnings and net financial items.  </p>
<p> Income before taxes	  391		 vs 370</p>
<p> Taxes			    154		 vs 149</p>
<p> Interest income		80		  vs 159</p>
<p> Interest expense	     164		 vs 215</p>
<p> Exchange differences	 1.0		 vs zero</p>
<p> Earnings from equity cos   1.0		 vs 1.0</p>
<p> Dividend income		1.0		 vs 1.0</p>
<p> Material expenses	    2,992	     vs 3,315</p>
<p> Personnel expenses	   2,387	     vs 2,532</p>
<p> Other expenses		 1,084	     vs 1,186</p>
<p>Changes, work in progress</p>
<p> and finished goods	   150		 vs 448</p>
<p> Fixed asset depreciation   248		 vs 260</p>
<p> Unusual items		  15		  vs 14</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
